Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||07-25-2000||01:03 PM||||Does any of you ever MANUALY SHIFT our AUTO transmission's????   I DO SOMETIMES..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I mean ... you know what I mean about shifting the auto transmission...at red light's ..  sometimes DOWN SHIFTING???? How BAD does it hurt it???  I found a 84 2m4 with a 4 speed in it.. WILL IT FIT  mine(87GT)????   thank's for any reply's that I get ...  Steve  85GT,87GT,842m4...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||07-25-2000||01:16 PM||||I do that in my Taurus sometimes.. seems to get slightly better acceleration, but when I shift back up... it acts like I've hit the gas in neutral.... tach jumps to 5,000 or so, and there's no acceleration.. so I gotta let off the gas and then slowly accelerate..<P>so.. manual shifting an automatic doesn't work good in a Taurus. however one of my friends does that in his Mustang, and it works fine.. same with another friend who has an 88 oldsmobile cutlass supreme.<P>Also, I drove Dave's 86GT (auto) in 2nd gear for a while, because I didn't notice it wasn't in 3rd.. (you really should fix that gear select indicator dave.. heh..)<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||07-25-2000||01:29 PM||||The only time I downshift my auto trans is if I want to slow down without hitting the brakes (example would be "IF" I was exceeding the speed limit and officer friendly was sitting on the side of the road) (Hint: if you are speeding and you see a police car then hit your brakes the officer now knows that you know you are speeding!) or if I want a little bit less downshift lag time I'll shift down to second gear then hit the gas to pass someone on the highway. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FieroGTRacingInc||07-25-2000||02:16 PM||||thank's for the reply's...   But Does it HURT the Transmission shifting it manually???||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||07-25-2000||02:28 PM||||It may depend on WHO you ask. I used to shift my 85 GT auto, 72 Cuda', 69 Firebird, 65 SS Nova and never had one break. I put 80,000 miles on the 85 GT auto and NEVER had a transmission problem. The only thing to watch out for is the temperature of the fluid. If it gets hot and turns brown... it's BAD! <P>In reality, transmissions that shift softly are harder on the clutches than one that has a shift kit installed to make it shift crisp (Or one that is shifted manually at higher RPMs). A soft shift allows the clutches to slip longer. The longer the shift the more friction. More friction means more heat. So I say, "shift away". Just watch the condition of the fluid and you should be fine.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000005||mrfixit58||07-25-2000||02:37 PM||||It may depend on WHO you ask. I used to shift my 85 GT auto, 72 Cuda', 69 Firebird, 65 SS Nova and never had one break. I put 80,000 miles on the 85 GT auto and NEVER had a transmission problem. The only thing to watch out for is the temperature of the fluid. If it gets hot and turns brown... it's BAD! <P>In reality, transmissions that shift softly are harder on the clutches than one that has a shift kit installed to make it shift crisp (Or one that is shifted manually at higher RPMs). A soft shift allows the clutches to slip longer. The longer the shift the more friction. More friction means more heat. So I say, "shift away". Just watch the condition of the fluid and you should be fine.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
